In [[computer programming]], a '''rope''', or '''cord''', is a [[data structure]] composed of smaller [[String (computer science)|strings]] that is used to efficiently store and manipulate a very long string. For example, a [[text editing]] program may use a rope to represent the text being edited, so that operations such as insertion, deletion, and random access can be done efficiently.<ref name="Boehm">
